  "description": "<h2>About the Project</h2>\n<p>IDCORE is an industry-linked doctoral training route in offshore renewable energy. The qualification is an EngD, with research and training connected to offshore energy challenges. Overseas applicants have a specific early deadline and a limited number of funded places.</p>\n<h2>Research Areas</h2>\n<ul><li>Offshore renewable energy</li><li>Engineering</li><li>Industrial research</li></ul>\n<h2>Funding and duration</h2>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin:14px 0;font-size:0.92em;line-height:1.45\"><thead style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;background:#eef3fb;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left\"><tr><th scope=\"col\" style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;background:#eef3fb;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left\">Component</th><th scope=\"col\" style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;background:#eef3fb;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left\">Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">Award or position</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">EngD studentship</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">Stipend / salary</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">Enhanced stipend plus tuition; amount not stated</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">Duration</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">Four-year EngD programme</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2>Eligibility and Requirements</h2>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin:14px 0;font-size:0.92em;line-height:1.45\"><thead style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;background:#eef3fb;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left\"><tr><th scope=\"col\" style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;background:#eef3fb;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left\">Criterion</th><th scope=\"col\" style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;background:#eef3fb;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left\">Requirement</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">Applicant eligibility</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">Worldwide, subject to programme rules</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">Further conditions</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">UK and overseas applicants; home closing dates differ; overseas places limited and ATAS may apply.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2>Application dates</h2>\n<table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin:14px 0;font-size:0.92em;line-height:1.45\"><thead style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;background:#eef3fb;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left\"><tr><th scope=\"col\" style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;background:#eef3fb;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left\">Component</th><th scope=\"col\" style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;background:#eef3fb;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left\">Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">Recruitment status</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">Open</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">Deadline / consideration round</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">30 November 2026 (overseas/EU applicants)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">Location</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #d9dee5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top\">United Kingdom</td></tr><tr></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2>About The University of Edinburgh</h2>\n<p>Edinburgh offers postgraduate research across science, engineering, humanities and health. Its collaborative doctoral programmes include industry-linked training, with admission and funding decisions made through the relevant programme.</p>\n<p><strong>Official details:</strong> <a href=\"https://idcore.ac.uk/information-applicants\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Read the programme or project information</a></p>\n<p><strong>Application route:</strong> <a href=\"https://idcore.ac.uk/information-applicants\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Follow the official application instructions</a></p>\n<h2>How to Apply</h2><p>Submit your application through the official portal before the deadline: 30 November 2026 (overseas/EU applicants). Read the eligibility requirements carefully and prepare all requested documents — early applications are strongly recommended for competitive awards.</p><p><a href=\"https://idcore.ac.uk/information-applicants\">Open the official application page ↗</a></p><h2>Application guides</h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"https://nextapply.co.uk/articles/how-to-read-phd-job-advertisement-before-applying\">How to Read a PhD Job Advert: Funding, Eligibility and Application Steps</a></li><li><a href=\"https://nextapply.co.uk/articles/how-to-write-academic-cv-phd-applications-sample\">Academic CV for PhD Applications: Structure and an Example</a></li></ul>",
